   "source": [
    "# TechCore · Análisis de ventas, catálogo y stock\n",
    "\n",
    "Análisis exploratorio de los reportes de la API de TechCore. Cada sección consulta un endpoint de `/reports`, muestra los datos en una tabla y un gráfico, y cierra con una breve lectura de los resultados.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requisitos**\n",
    "1. API corriendo: `python app.py` (con la base cargada con `python seed.py`).\n",
    "2. Librerías: `pip install pandas matplotlib requests`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contenido**\n",
    "1. Resumen general\n",
    "2. Evolución mensual de las ventas\n",
    "3. Desempeño de los vendedores\n",
    "4. Ventas por línea de producto\n",
    "5. Computadoras más vendidas\n",
    "6. Mejores clientes\n",
    "7. Unidades por venta\n",
    "8. Catálogo por rango de precio\n",
    "9. Inventario de componentes por categoría\n",
    "10. Componentes más usados y riesgo de stock\n",
    "11. Conclusiones"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df9f4706",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuración"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "320ad5cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "API_URL = \"http://localhost:5000\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def get(path, **params):\n",
    "    \"\"\"GET to the API. Returns the JSON response (list or dict).\"\"\"\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = requests.get(f\"{API_URL}{path}\", params=params, timeout=10)\n",
    "    except requests.ConnectionError:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not connect to {API_URL}. Is the API running? (python app.py)\")\n",
    "    response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "    return response.json()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_df(path, **params):\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(get(path, **params))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- chart style\n",
    "BLUE, BLUE_LIGHT, GRAY, RED = \"#2a78d6\", \"#9ec5f4\", \"#c3c2b7\", \"#d03b3b\"\n",
    "INK, INK_2 = \"#0b0b0b\", \"#52514e\"\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.figsize\": (9, 4), \"figure.dpi\": 110,\n",
    "    \"figure.facecolor\": \"#fcfcfb\", \"axes.facecolor\": \"#fcfcfb\",\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "    \"axes.edgecolor\": GRAY, \"axes.labelcolor\": INK_2,\n",
    "    \"axes.titlesize\": 13, \"axes.titleweight\": \"bold\", \"axes.titlecolor\": INK,\n",
    "    \"axes.titlelocation\": \"left\", \"axes.titlepad\": 12,\n",
    "    \"xtick.color\": INK_2, \"ytick.color\": INK_2,\n",
    "    \"axes.grid\": True, \"grid.color\": \"#e6e5e0\", \"grid.linewidth\": 0.8,\n",
    "    \"axes.axisbelow\": True, \"font.size\": 10,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Axis format: $45k instead of $45,000 so ticks don't overlap in narrow charts\n",
    "money = mticker.FuncFormatter(lambda x, _: f\"${x / 1000:,.0f}k\" if abs(x) >= 1000 else f\"${x:,.0f}\")\n",
    "MONTHS = [\"Ene\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Abr\", \"May\", \"Jun\", \"Jul\", \"Ago\", \"Sep\", \"Oct\", \"Nov\", \"Dic\"]\n",
    "MONTHS_LONG = [\"enero\", \"febrero\", \"marzo\", \"abril\", \"mayo\", \"junio\", \"julio\", \"agosto\",\n",
    "               \"septiembre\", \"octubre\", \"noviembre\", \"diciembre\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def label_bar(ax, bar, text, horizontal=True):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Value label at the end of a single bar.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if horizontal:\n",
    "        ax.annotate(text, (bar.get_width(), bar.get_y() + bar.get_height() / 2),\n",
    "                    xytext=(4, 0), textcoords=\"offset points\", va=\"center\", fontsize=9, color=INK)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        ax.annotate(text, (bar.get_x() + bar.get_width() / 2, bar.get_height()),\n",
    "                    xytext=(0, 3), textcoords=\"offset points\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=9, color=INK)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def hbar(ax, labels, values, highlight=None, colors=None, fmt=\"{:,.0f}\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Horizontal bars, largest on top. The highlighted bar is blue, the rest light blue.\n",
    "    Only the highlighted bar gets a value label; the table above has every value.\"\"\"\n",
    "    labels, values = list(labels)[::-1], list(values)[::-1]\n",
    "    if colors is None:\n",
    "        top = len(values) - 1 if highlight is None else len(values) - 1 - highlight\n",
    "        colors = [BLUE if i == top else BLUE_LIGHT for i in range(len(values))]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        colors = list(colors)[::-1]\n",
    "    bars = ax.barh(labels, values, color=colors, height=0.65, edgecolor=\"#fcfcfb\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n",
    "    if highlight is not None:\n",
    "        i = len(values) - 1 - highlight\n",
    "        label_bar(ax, bars[i], fmt.format(values[i]))\n",
    "    return bars"
   ]
  },
